A.ReleaseNotes={version="1.2.7",changes={"Long cross-continent trips, including Stormwind to Desolace, prioritise walking connections that advance the whole journey, cutting down on unnecessary searches.","If a same-zone pin falls outside mapped walking terrain, smart routing automatically looks for connected ground within 80 yards. It shows how far the route ends from your pin.","At Booty Bay, follow the arrow to the Ratchet ferry plank at 26.0, 73.2. Arriving by a different boardwalk also switches guidance from walking to boarding.","The route-planning popup counts down before closing. Completed routes stay visible for five seconds and cancelled calculations for three. Errors stay open so you can copy a report.","Flight-master pins show a green check for confirmed stops, a padlock for stops the game marks undiscovered, and a plain boot when status is uncertain. Hover for details.","Opening a flight map confirms the current stop and reachable destinations for that character, avoiding false green checks on unlearned stops.","Escape now closes the world map during combat. Press Escape again to open the game menu.","Audited roads, bridges and tunnels in six capitals and improved bridge-floor detection tools. The audit documents remaining gaps in Stormwind, Ironforge and other cities."}}
